        beleg: "Wolfgang Beltracchi forged the works of well-known artists for decades with a stylistic fusion so thorough it fooled even experts; Ed Gein, after the death of his extremely dominant mother, spent years opening the graves of older women to literally \"slip into\" their identity through their remains – the same fusion logic as Beltracchi's, here not with the style of dead masters but with the body of his dead mother, derailed into fatal psychosis. Bernard Eugene Giles shows a third variant of the same underlying movement: his merging attached to no real, individual other, as with Gein, but to an interchangeable, anonymous image of complete strangers – he himself stated he could not have killed anyone he knew personally, because only the victim's total impersonality left the merging fantasy undisturbed."
