function triadendefizitePage() {
  return shell(`
    ${pageHeader("triadendefizite")}
    <div style="max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1rem 3rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Charts &middot; Triads</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Triad Deficits</h1>
      <h2 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin:-.4rem 0 1.2rem;letter-spacing:.03em;">Protection &middot; Love &middot; Trust</h2>
      <p class="psycho-intro">In the Enneagram, the nine types can be organized into three basic centers: gut, heart, and head. These centers describe less behavior and more the primary way a person processes reality and reacts to a perceived core deficit. The gut triad is characterized by a protection deficit, the heart triad by a love deficit, and the head triad by a trust deficit. The different strategies of the individual types unfold from these core tensions.</p>

      <img src="../assets/triadendefizite-1.png" alt="Triadendefizite Schaubild 1"
        style="width:100%;border-radius:12px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;display:block;" />
      <img src="../assets/triadendefizite-2.png" alt="Triadendefizite Schaubild 2"
        style="width:100%;border-radius:12px;margin:0 auto 2.5rem;display:block;" />

      <div class="vb-section" style="max-width:100%;">

        <div class="vb-typ">
          <h3 class="vb-typ__head" style="color:#8b5e3c;"><span class="vb-typ__nr" style="background:#8b5e3c;">Gut Triad</span> Types 8, 9, and 1 &ndash; Protection Deficit</h3>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">The gut types organize themselves around the theme of protection and integrity. The unconscious inner question is: <em>Am I safe, intact, unassailable?</em></p>
          <div style="display:grid;gap:.5rem;font-size:.85rem;margin:.7rem 0;line-height:1.65;">
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 8</span> compensates for the protection deficit through overcompensation: strength, control, and assertiveness, so that vulnerability never becomes noticeable in the first place. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Protection through strength.</span></div>
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 9</span> protects itself by numbing tension: conflict is avoided, inner deflation stabilizes harmony. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Protection through calm.</span></div>
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 1</span> seeks protection through order: a reliable world in which errors, chaos, and moral inconsistency are reduced. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Protection through correctness.</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">All three gut types struggle for intactness &mdash; yet one protects through power, another through calm, the third through order.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vb-typ">
          <h3 class="vb-typ__head" style="color:#b05080;"><span class="vb-typ__nr" style="background:#b05080;">Heart Triad</span> Types 2, 3, and 4 &ndash; Love Deficit</h3>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">The heart types revolve around a love deficit. The inner question is: <em>Am I lovable, valuable, seen?</em></p>
          <div style="display:grid;gap:.5rem;font-size:.85rem;margin:.7rem 0;line-height:1.65;">
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 2</span> tries to secure love through giving: attentive, supportive, caring. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Love through closeness.</span></div>
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 3</span> strives for achievement and recognition, because admiration is experienced as a substitute for love. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Love through success.</span></div>
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 4</span> seeks deep, authentic resonance &mdash; to be seen at one's innermost core. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Love through authenticity.</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">All three heart types struggle for the certainty of love &mdash; yet one seeks it through giving, another through achievement, the third through identity.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vb-typ">
          <h3 class="vb-typ__head" style="color:#3a6b8a;"><span class="vb-typ__nr" style="background:#3a6b8a;">Head Triad</span> Types 5, 6, and 7 &ndash; Trust Deficit</h3>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">The head types are shaped by a trust deficit. The inner question is: <em>Can I trust the world, others, and myself?</em></p>
          <div style="display:grid;gap:.5rem;font-size:.85rem;margin:.7rem 0;line-height:1.65;">
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 5</span> builds up knowledge, clarity, and mental autonomy to reduce uncertainty. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Trust through competence.</span></div>
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 6</span> checks, doubts, anticipates risks, and seeks reliability in structures and loyalties. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Trust through security.</span></div>
            <div><span style="font-weight:700;color:var(--copper);">Type 7</span> keeps options open and orients itself toward the future and freedom to evade constriction and pain. <span style="color:var(--muted);">Trust through openness.</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">All three head types struggle with insecurity &mdash; yet one counters it with knowledge, another with security-seeking, the third with freedom.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.6rem;margin-top:1rem;">
          <p class="vb-intro">Thus, three basic movements reveal themselves: protection, love, and trust. The gut types seek intactness, the heart types seek the certainty of love, the head types seek reliability. Every type is a specific response to a perceived deficit. It is not the visible behavior that is decisive, but the underlying movement with which the system repeatedly attempts to regulate its core insecurity.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-left:3px solid var(--gold);padding:.9rem 1.1rem;margin:1.8rem 0;background:var(--paper);border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.8;font-style:italic;">May these charts and the accompanying text help you see the three inner centers even more clearly and walk your own path within them with more understanding, depth, and friendly alertness.</p>
        </div>

        ${relatedLinks([
          {route:"schutzdefizite", label:"Protection Deficits"},
          {route:"grundformel", label:"Core Formula of the Rathmer Enneagram"},
          {route:"drei-zentren", label:"Three Centers"},
          {route:"energiestatus-triadenenergien", label:"Energy Status of the Triad Energies"},
        ])}
      </div>
    </div>
  `);
}

